ird term: - [ sin\u00b2 alpha sin 3alpha ] / [ sin 2alpha cos alpha ]\n\nLet\u2019s express sin 3alpha in terms of sin alpha and cos alpha:\n\nsin 3alpha = 3 sin alpha - 4 sin^3 alpha\n\nBut this may not help. Alternatively, express in terms of sin 2alpha and alpha:\n\nsin 3alpha = sin(2alpha + alpha ) = sin 2alpha cos alpha + cos 2alpha sin alpha\n\nTherefore, sin 3alpha = sin 2alpha cos alpha + cos 2alpha sin alpha\n\nSimilarly, sin 2alpha = 2 sin alpha cos alpha\n\nLet\u2019s substitute sin 3alpha into the first term:\n\nFirst term: [ sin\u00b2 alpha (sin 2alpha cos alpha + cos 2alpha sin alpha )\u00b2 ] / [ sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha ]\n\nExpand the numerator:\n\n(sin 2alpha cos alpha + cos 2alpha sin alpha )\u00b2 = sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha + 2 sin 2alpha cos alpha cos 2alpha sin alpha + cos\u00b2 2alpha sin\u00b2 alpha\n\nTherefore, first term becomes:\n\nsin\u00b2 alpha [ sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha + 2 sin 2alpha cos alpha cos 2alpha sin alpha + cos\u00b2 2alpha sin\u00b2 alpha ] / ( sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha )\n\nDivide each term by denominator:\n\n= sin\u00b2 alpha [ sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha / sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha + 2 sin 2alpha cos alpha cos 2alpha sin alpha / sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha + cos\u00b2 2alpha sin\u00b2 alpha / sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha ]\n\n= sin\u00b2 alpha [ 1 + (2 cos 2alpha sin alpha ) / ( sin 2alpha cos alpha ) + (cos\u00b2 2alpha sin\u00b2 alpha ) / ( sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha ) ]\n\nSimplify each term:\n\nSecond term inside: 2 cos 2alpha sin alpha / ( sin 2alpha cos alpha ) = 2 cos 2alpha sin alpha / ( 2 sin alpha cos alpha * cos alpha ) = cos 2alpha / cos\u00b2 alpha\n\nThird term: cos\u00b2 2alpha sin\u00b2 alpha / ( sin\u00b2 2alpha cos\u00b2 alpha ) = [ cos\u00b2 2alpha / sin\u00b2 2alpha ] * [ sin\u00b2 alpha / cos\u00b2 alpha ] = cot\u00b2 2alpha * tan\u00b2 alpha\n\nTherefore, first term becomes:\n\nsin\u00b2 alpha [ 1 + (cos 2alpha / cos\u00b2 alpha ) + cot\u00b2