\n2D_x = 1.5H_x - (\u221a3/2)H_y + \u221a3 D_y -1\n\nSimilarly, process the second equation:\n\n2D_y = (\u221a3/2)H_x + 1.5H_y - (\u221a3/2)*(1.5D_x + 0.5 - (\u221a3/2)D_y) - 0.5*(1.5D_y + (\u221a3/2)D_x - (\u221a3/2))\n\nCompute each term:\n\nFirst term: (\u221a3/2)H_x\n\nSecond term: 1.5H_y\n\nThird term: - (\u221a3/2)*(1.5D_x) - (\u221a3/2)*(0.5) + (\u221a3/2)*(\u221a3/2 D_y )\n\n= - (3\u221a3/4)D_x - (\u221a3/4) + (3/4)D_y\n\nFourth term: -0.5*(1.5D_y) -0.5*(\u221a3/2 D_x ) +0.5*(\u221a3/2)\n\n= -0.75D_y - (\u221a3/4 D_x ) + (\u221a3/4)\n\nCombine all terms:\n\n2D_y = (\u221a3/2)H_x + 1.5H_y - (3\u221a3/4)D_x - (\u221a3/4) + (3/4)D_y -0.75D_y - (\u221a3/4 D_x ) + (\u221a3/4)\n\nSimplify:\n\nLeft side: 2D_y\n\nRight side:\n\n(\u221a3/2)H_x + 1.5H_y\n\n+ (-3\u221a3/4 D_x - \u221a3/4 D_x ) = - (4\u221a3/4 )D_x = -\u221a3 D_x\n\n+ (-\u221a3/4 + \u221a3/4 ) = 0\n\n+ (3/4 D_y - 0.75 D_y ) = (3/4 - 3/4 )D_y = 0\n\nTherefore:\n\n2D_y = (\u221a3/2)H_x + 1.5H_y - \u221a3 D_x\n\nSo now we have two equations:\n\n1. 2D_x = 1.5H_x - (\u221a3/2)H_y + \u221a3 D_y -1\n\n2. 2D_y = (\u221a3/2)H_x + 1.5H_y - \u221a3 D_x\n\nThese are two equations with variables H_x and H_y. Let me try to solve for H_x and H_y.\n\nLet me denote equation 1 as:\n\n1.5H_x - (\u221a3/2)H_y = 2D_x - \u221a3 D_y +1  --- (1)\n\nEquation 2 as:\n\n(\u221a3/2)H_x + 1.5H_y = 2D_y + \u221a3 D_x --- (2)\n\nLet me write these equations in matrix form:\n\n[1.5        -\u221a3/2      ] [H_x]   = [2D_x - \u221a3 D_y +1]\n\n[\u221a3/2        1.5       ] [H_y]     [2D_y + \u221a3 D_x ]\n\nTo solve this system, we can use Cramer's rule or find the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\nFirst, compute the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n\u0394 = (1.5)(1.5) - (-\u221a3/2)(\u221a3/2) = 2.25 - ( - (3/4) ) = 2.25 + 0.75 = 3\n\nSo determinant \u0394 = 3.\n\nThe inverse matrix is (1/\u0394) * [1.5        \u221a3/2      ]\n\n                             [-\u221a3/2      1.5       ]\n\nSo, the inverse is (1/3) times:\n